{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 15, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "Stepping off the plane in Tokyo, I was immediately swept up in a whirlwind of neon lights and ancient tradition. My journey began in the bustling heart of Shibuya, where the famous crossing feels like a choreographed dance of thousands. Yet, just a short train ride away, the chaos faded into the serene silence of the Meiji Shrine, surrounded by a towering forest in the middle of the city.\n\nNext, I traveled to Kyoto to witness a different side of Japan. Walking through the thousands of vermilion torii gates at Fushimi Inari Taisha at sunrise was magical; the path seemed to lead straight into another world. I spent my afternoon in the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove, where the swaying stalks created a natural symphony with the wind.\n\nNo trip to Japan is complete without the food. From steaming bowls of ramen in tiny alleyway shops to the delicate art of sushi in a quiet Ginza restaurant, every meal was an adventure. The attention to detail in every dish was breathtaking.\n\nOne evening, I visited an onsen in the countryside. Soaking in the hot mineral waters under a blanket of stars, watching snow gently fall on the cedar trees, I felt a profound sense of peace. It was a perfect blend of relaxation and connection with nature.\n\nAs I boarded my flight home, my heart was full. Japan is a country where the future and the past coexist harmoniously. Whether you are chasing the quiet of a temple or the energy of a city street, this island nation offers an unforgettable experience that lingers long after you leave.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ste", "logprob": -2.2552052}, {"token": "pping", "logprob": -1.192093e-07}, {"token": " off", "logprob": -0.028888324}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " plane", "logprob": -0.033173393}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.0009498934}, {"token": " Tokyo", "logprob": -0.0005054559}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.3535355}, {